  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Nutrition and Health Activity (CNHA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  Community Support Groups (CSGs), 2) Community Groups (CGs), and 3) Core Teams (Local Health Managers). It will employ supportive supervision to ensure quality services and outreach meet expected standards. With FY 2024 funds, CNHA will revitalize CSGs and CGs to conduct community outreach and courtyard sessions per the Government of Bangladesh&apos;s CSG manual. This will include training 21,063 CG members, 51,425 CSG members, 750 Core Team members, and 5,364 Community Champions. Community champions will conduct monthly community outreach sessions to connect to services, and promote referral and follow-up. It will engage adolescent clubs with school campaigns. CNHA will  engage with existing platforms to improve nutrition and health outcomes, targeting: 1) strategic support to Severe Acute Malnutrition (SAM) Management Committees, with district Core Teams, to address SAM management barriers and also  build the capacity of 156 SAM Management Committee members and develop a national-level Growth Monitoring and Promotion dashboard to track and follow-up SAM cases. In sub-district facilities, CNHA will strengthen water, sanitation and hygiene; maternal and child services; family planning counseling; and screen for chronic diseases linked to nutrition. CNHA will partner with USAID&apos;s Bangladesh Nutrition Activity; other national and sub-national stakeholders; and the private sector for resilience, food safety, and food security.  FY 2024 funding will contribute to Adaptation Indirect ($1m), SL Indirect ($400k),Innovation ($50k) Gender Equality ($950k), GBV ($450k),GBV-CEFM ($150k), GFS ($5.2m), Health Workforce ($500k), Cross-Cutting HSS ($2.35m), MSN ($5.2m),(Macronutrients ($1.4m of which Vit A is $1.1m), PGI-Indirect Health ($3.55m), WASH ($300k) issues. The activity will support the JSP FY 2022-2026 Goal Three, with the U.S. government&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective  3.1 Improved human capital, particularly in health and education.</narrative>
  </description>
